                        "form_id": "0927ab2f-055e-4e83-b68a-38c4ec02f659",
                        "entry_id": "37092113-28df-31f5-9165-4013f7b4072f",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more whiskery"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "43d22ee9-81de-45f6-99f6-ceac990e01cd",
                        "entry_id": "37092113-28df-31f5-9165-4013f7b4072f",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most whiskery"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eba5030c-eb11-39e0-aef4-5bc8746923c2",
                        "entry_id": "37092113-28df-31f5-9165-4013f7b4072f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having whiskers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4bb5496-11f8-4ca8-9a20-5fb47853c2d8",
                                "sense_id": "eba5030c-eb11-39e0-aef4-5bc8746923c2",
                                "text": "[T]he old lady is as ugly as any woman in the parish, and as tall and whiskery as a Grenadier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95297c3d-7e24-4cc1-bb34-03473767c250",
                                "sense_id": "eba5030c-eb11-39e0-aef4-5bc8746923c2",
                                "text": "\"Don't you my-dear me,\" she sniffed. \"I don't like you.\" / \"Why?\" / \"Cos …\" She ladled the punch carefully into the mugs and meditated. \"Cos you chew tobacco. Cos you're whiskery. Wot I take to is smooth-faced young chaps.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e722755a-0b99-4542-a97f-f080701608d3",
                                "sense_id": "eba5030c-eb11-39e0-aef4-5bc8746923c2",
                                "text": "At a corner table two whiskery ranch hands were playing checkers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09915ba6-9e12-426e-938b-df01b223e05a",
                                "sense_id": "eba5030c-eb11-39e0-aef4-5bc8746923c2",
                                "text": "I looked at Dr Grene and tried to imagine him altered by the moon, more whiskery, a werewolf possibly."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1d9b57c1-6458-3d0a-8cba-2ca40c5e5cc4",
                        "entry_id": "37092113-28df-31f5-9165-4013f7b4072f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having protrusions resembling whiskers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa19b0ec-b088-4d8d-a7d0-5c4f0d1283d7",
                                "sense_id": "1d9b57c1-6458-3d0a-8cba-2ca40c5e5cc4",
                                "text": "Smiling, he gave us a salute, turned his horse and rode down the trail, through the high hairy weeds and whiskery flowers thriving among the rocks and faded ruts of the road."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e42442b8-945e-449f-a98e-c4dd8879bb4e",
                                "sense_id": "1d9b57c1-6458-3d0a-8cba-2ca40c5e5cc4",
                                "text": "The whiskery batfish (a kind of anglerfish) is covered with outgrowths of skin that resemble bits of seaweed."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a4bab1b8-13e1-3e95-9be8-8d276dc8ebf6",
                        "entry_id": "37092113-28df-31f5-9165-4013f7b4072f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling whiskers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c2ee1c8-8e8e-48a5-8e56-4fcca4f4fe82",
                                "sense_id": "a4bab1b8-13e1-3e95-9be8-8d276dc8ebf6",
                                "text": "[…] all the white trees, tall like poles, that went up and up to where, right at the top, among whiskery branches, were bits of blue that were the sky."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37156ee0-d82e-43a9-9110-5ca316b93494",
                                "sense_id": "a4bab1b8-13e1-3e95-9be8-8d276dc8ebf6",
                                "text": "He nodded his head toward an ancient armchair spewing out its whiskery stuffing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "120d9fad-c74b-4f45-a792-3abbf1b8b02c",
                                "sense_id": "a4bab1b8-13e1-3e95-9be8-8d276dc8ebf6",
                                "text": "At first, all he sees is a harmless-looking blob, a microscopic single-cell organism sporting a couple of whiskery flagella."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a8a644b5-ae80-32d8-bfb7-df73da745d93",
                        "entry_id": "37092113-28df-31f5-9165-4013f7b4072f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Involving or caused by whiskers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0da22c90-fde8-40c6-a77d-e239bfab88a2",
                                "sense_id": "a8a644b5-ae80-32d8-bfb7-df73da745d93",
                                "text": "He bent his great, shaggy head over Harry and gave him what must have been a very scratchy, whiskery kiss."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13b9a3e3-a00b-4d67-9888-78cfcbf1b61d",
                                "sense_id": "a8a644b5-ae80-32d8-bfb7-df73da745d93",
                                "text": "2002, Jeffrey Eugenides, Middlesex, New York: Picador, Book Three, “Flesh and Blood,” p. 373,\nDespite my lightheadedness, I could feel everything. The shocking wetness of his mouth. The whiskery feel of his lips. His barging tongue."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5388ec47-1e62-30c5-95b4-b50808fcbc38",
                        "entry_id": "37092113-28df-31f5-9165-4013f7b4072f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Old."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "humorous"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6acfff07-7993-4e13-946e-abd24ab49c93",
                                "sense_id": "5388ec47-1e62-30c5-95b4-b50808fcbc38",
                                "text": "It is, of course, the most whiskery old cliché, but clichés usually have their basis in fact, and this one certainly does: Historically, the French have paid extraordinary—some would say excessive—attention to what they eat and how they eat it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80faa1fe-41f3-4940-a84d-0d0df6e22411",
                                "sense_id": "5388ec47-1e62-30c5-95b4-b50808fcbc38",
                                "text": "I checked it out, and there were some good—if whiskery—stories."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
